WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.354 --> 00:00:06.306
Excel MCP Server lets your AI assistant work in the real Excel desktop app.

2
00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:08.923
Ask in plain English. Excel does the work.

3
00:00:09.657 --> 00:00:14.649
File-based tools are useful for creating and editing spreadsheets without Excel.

4
00:00:14.749 --> 00:00:20.338
Anthropic's spreadsheet skill uses openpyxl, with LibreOffice for calculation.

5
00:00:20.438 --> 00:00:27.243
Excel MCP uses Microsoft's Excel engine instead, including the features built into the app.

6
00:00:27.782 --> 00:00:33.137
Use it for refreshable reports, complex existing workbooks, and live Excel results.

7
00:00:33.237 --> 00:00:39.040
For simple exports, or work without Windows and Excel, file-based tools may be the better fit.

8
00:00:39.719 --> 00:00:41.447
Start with one sales workbook.

9
00:00:41.547 --> 00:00:44.555
Ask your assistant to turn raw orders into a report.

10
00:00:44.655 --> 00:00:47.642
Or drive the same workflow with excelcli.

11
00:00:48.836 --> 00:00:52.527
Power Query turns preparation into a repeatable process.

12
00:00:52.627 --> 00:00:57.150
Clean the source, shape your sales data, and refresh the query inside Excel.

13
00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:58.637
Not a static export.

14
00:01:00.877 --> 00:01:03.096
Bring those tables into the Data Model.

15
00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:08.849
Define revenue once with DAX, then reuse that business logic across your analysis.

16
00:01:08.949 --> 00:01:10.570
The model stays in your workbook.

17
00:01:13.387 --> 00:01:15.627
Build a PivotTable to compare regions.

18
00:01:15.727 --> 00:01:18.010
Add a chart, and the story becomes clear.

19
00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:21.737
These are native Excel objects, ready for the next question.

20
00:01:24.555 --> 00:01:26.283
Already have a trusted workflow?

21
00:01:26.383 --> 00:01:28.559
Work with VBA modules and macros.

22
00:01:28.659 --> 00:01:32.094
Run only trusted macros. They have your user permissions.

23
00:01:33.416 --> 00:01:35.208
Go further with Python in Excel.

24
00:01:35.308 --> 00:01:37.100
Write analysis beside your data.

25
00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:42.320
Python runs in Microsoft's cloud, with a supported subscription and internet access.

26
00:01:43.439 --> 00:01:46.319
Change an input. Excel calculates the result.

27
00:01:46.419 --> 00:01:51.283
Keep the formulas, queries, charts, and workbook features that make the file valuable.

28
00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:56.216
For coding agents, excelcli can use fewer tokens.

29
00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:59.281
Two equal ways in. One real Excel engine.
